 "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-1/trig-omp-reported/29/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass (`test_dates`, `test_naive`, `test_day_key`).\n\n**Cause:** the format string `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` has nothing to match a trailing `Z` (UTC), so `strptime` stopped with that error.\n\n**Fix:** it now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`, which accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 and later. This repo runs Python 3.13.5.\n\n**Behavior change:** a timestamp ending in `Z` or a `\u00b1HH:MM` offset now comes back carrying its timezone (UTC for `Z`). One without an offset still comes back without a timezone, as before. Python raises a `TypeError` if you compare or subtract the two kinds, so a caller that mixes them could break. The only callers in the repo are `day_key` and the tests, and neither does that. I noted this in the docstring.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 52909, "requests_cache_write": 131983, "requests_cost_usd": 0.6985607999999999, "requests_count": 7, "requests_